message: "If you use engmolines in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "engmolines: the numerical method of lines for engineering PDEs, in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Yanwei
    email: wangyanwei@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8488-9833"
    website: "https://github.com/ktwyw"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ktwyw/engmolines"
keywords:
  - method of lines
  - partial differential equations
  - stiff ODEs
  - finite differences
  - finite volumes
  - spectral methods
  - scientific computing
  - engineering education
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch, validated implementation of the numerical method of lines for engineering PDEs: stencils with
  matched boundary closures, ghost-point boundary conditions, conservative and flux-limited operators, Fourier
  spectral derivatives, stiffness analysis, and explicit, implicit (banded Newton), IMEX, symplectic and DAE
  time integrators, with 37 example problems checked against exact solutions and benchmarks and a 16-notebook
  course with worked solutions.
